put.description:
Update user preferences.

Merges the provided preferences with existing preferences.
Does not replace the entire preferences object.
Requires authentication.

Example request:
{
  "preferences": {
    "tutorial_completed": true,
    "daily_digest_theme": "dark"
  }
}

post.description:
Read a specific resource by ID.

Example:
```json
{
    "resource_type": "company-profile",
    "resource_id": "123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000",
    "params": {"include_products": true}
}
```

List available resources of a specific type.

Example:
```json
{
    "resource_type": "company-profile",
    "params": {"limit": 10, "offset": 0}
}
```

Execute an MCP tool.

Example:
```json
{
    "tool_name": "generate_campaign_ideas",
    "company_profile_id": "123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000",
    "arguments": {
        "customer_goal": "increase brand awareness",
        "target_audiences": [
            {"description": "Tech-savvy millennials"}
        ]
    }
}
```

get.description:
SSE endpoint for real-time job progress.

Stream format:
    event: started
    data: {"job_id": "...", "job_type": "...", "timestamp": "..."}

    event: progress
    data: {"step": "...", "message": "...", "progress": 0.5}

    event: completed
    data: {"job_id": "...", "result": {...}, "duration_seconds": 45.2}

    event: failed
    data: {"job_id": "...", "error": "...", "error_type": "..."}

Per Issue #271 specification.
